**: The test failed as it cannot locate the "Logout" link element, indicating that the logout functionality is not implemented in the user interface.\n   - **Improvement Guidance**: Develop a logout feature that is accessible in the user interface, such as adding a logout link in the dashboard template. Ensure the link is properly routed to trigger session termination, removing the user from the current session and redirecting them back to the login page. This creates a seamless experience for users and confirms the functionality\'s presence on the page.\n   - **Error Analysis**: The test attempted to click a "Logout" link that was not available to the user, leading to a `NoSuchElementException`.\n   - **Improvement Guidance**: Implement a logout functionality that allows users to log out and redirects them back to the login page. Ensure that after logging in, the "Logout" link appears on all pages as required, and the session is cleared appropriately. It¡¯s important to establish user navigation throughout the application correctly.']
